# Named people at holdings, the hub (docs/DIALOGUE.md, "Hubs: work comes out of talk"): their errand
# ("Anything need doing?", slot 1) comes out of their own work, and "Ask how things are" (slot 0) out
# of what's going round. Each speaks for their faction and their job; persona:1-3 keeps two of one
# job apart. Some of what's going round is wrong, and somebody else knows it.
# Each faction has a first meeting greet (who they are, where you are, the place's rules), once a
# life per person; greet lines are conditional, so the talk screen shows only what says something.

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ The Haven
conv named.haven.intro
for named:haven
when !exiled & !hunted:haven
greet
prio world
once
voice haven

node start
  say? !met & role:farmer :: You're on Haven ground, at {here}. I keep the fields, what's left of them. What grows here goes to the safehouses, so mind where you put your boots.
  say? !met & role:nurse :: You've come to {here}, a Haven holding. I'm the nurse. If you're hurt, say so. If you're bitten, say so louder. Nobody's turned away for either.
  say? !met & role:cook :: You've found {here}, a Haven holding, and its kitchen, which is me. Everyone works and everyone eats. You can start with either, but I'd start with eating.
  say? !met & role:lookout :: I saw you coming a mile off. You're at {here}, a Haven holding. I keep the watch. Walk in slow, keep your gun down, and you're welcome.
  say? !met :: You're at {here}, a Haven holding. We're ordinary people who decided to help each other, because nobody outside the line is going to. Everyone works here.

conv named.haven.work
for named:haven
when !exiled & !hunted:haven
topic "How's the day treating you?"
prio ask
voice haven

node start
  say? role:farmer & rain :: Rain. The beans like it. The fence posts don't. Neither do I, much. I've been out since five turning soil for potatoes that might feed a house in a month, if a month comes.
  say? role:farmer :: Turned a row by hand. The tractor wants fuel, the fuel wants a truck, and the truck wants a road without the Red Hand's toll on it. So I've got a spade.
  say? role:nurse & persona:1 :: Two fevers and a cut that's just a cut. I checked it three times, because everyone's frightened of every cut now. It's just a cut. I told him twice and he still cried.
  say? role:nurse :: Boiled the bandages again. They're more boil than bandage now. There's no new gauze anywhere in {here}, so the old stuff goes round and round.
  say? role:cook :: Soup. Then soup. Someone asked me for bread this morning and I laughed until I had to sit down. There's no flour within a day's walk, and no oven that'd take it.
  say? role:lookout :: Long. Nothing moved on the roads. Nothing moving is the best kind of day up there, and the most tiring, because you can't stop looking for the thing that will.
  say Long. They're all long now. We work the holding so the safehouses have something to eat, and every day there's a little more to do and a few less hands to do it.
  > @what What would make it easier? -> ask
  > @nurse Who are you most worried about? -> worried   if role:nurse
  > @how How are things here, generally? -> hub   do call:slot:0
  > @no I'll let you get on. -> hub

node worried
  say The quiet one by the window. He hasn't eaten in two days. Says he isn't hungry. Nobody in the Zone is not hungry. He's giving his bowl away, and I can't prove it.
  > @help Is there anything I can do? -> ask
  > @back1 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

node ask
  say? persona:2 :: Honestly? Another pair of hands. We've water to fetch, tins to find, a gate to keep at dusk. Ask me properly and I'll tell you what's true today, and what it's worth.
  say Something always needs doing. The Haven runs on favours, and we pay in kind: a little Favor with the houses, a hot meal, a name people say kindly. Ask, and I'll say if it's real.
  > @take I'll help. What needs doing? -> hub   do call:slot:1
  > @later Not right now. Later. -> hub

conv named.haven.word
for named:haven
when !exiled & !hunted:haven
topic "What's the talk round here?"
prio world
voice haven

bind hungry = news:hungry
bind lost = news:lost_by(bastion)
bind took = news:taken
bind who = news:taken_by

node start
  jump news:hungry -> hungry
  jump news:lost_by(bastion) -> withdrew
  jump news:taken -> taken
  say? epilogue :: That it's ending. People say it at the door like the weather: the checkpoints are processing, the cure's out, we're going home. Nobody quite believes the last part.
  say? need:food :: That supper's thin everywhere, not just here. Every house in the network's on short rations. That helps, oddly. Nobody likes being the only hungry house.
  say Nothing worth repeating. Which never stops anyone repeating it. The Haven's houses talk to each other by radio and by notes on doors, and most of it's about food.
  > @me What do people say about me? -> me
  > @how And here? How are things? -> hub   do call:slot:0
  > @back0 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

node hungry
  say That {bind:hungry} is on half portions. The children eat first there too. That part never changes, whichever house you're in. It's the one rule nobody's ever broken.
  > @how1 And how are things here? -> hub   do call:slot:0
  > @back1 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

node withdrew
  say That Bastion lost {bind:lost}. Lost it, mind. A man came through yesterday with his hand burned to the wrist who was there when it went. He saw the soldiers run for the trucks. ~truth:gossip.withdrew@lost
  say Bastion won't say it like that. They'll say something with a lot of long words and a time in it, like it happened on purpose.
  > @how2 And how are things here? -> hub   do call:slot:0
  > @back2 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

node taken
  say That {bind:who} has {bind:took} now. The flag changed on the pole. The families there didn't. They'll still need feeding, whoever's counting the tins.
  > @how3 And how are things here? -> hub   do call:slot:0
  > @back3 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

node me
  jump kit:other -> me_colours
  say? best:haven :: That you {best}. They say it like they were there. Half of them weren't. It goes round the houses, and it'll get bigger every time it's told. That's how we thank people.
  say? tier:haven>=known :: That you're all right. That's high praise in the Haven. We're sparing with praise. It's cheaper than soup, but we like to make it last.
  say Nothing yet. You're a coat and a pair of boots so far. Do something for one of the houses and they'll talk about you at supper. That's how you get a name here.
  > @back4 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

node me_colours
  say That you're wearing someone else's colours. Polite people asked whose. Less polite people guessed. The Haven doesn't mind what you wear, but it notices.
  > @back5 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ Bastion
conv named.bastion.intro
for named:bastion
when !hunted:bastion
greet
prio world
once
voice bastion

node start
  say? !met & role:sentry :: Halt there. Right. You're at {here}, Bastion post. I'm on the sentry rota. Hands where the tower can see them, and nobody crosses the wire without a word. Then we'll get on.
  say? !met & role:radio_operator :: You're at {here}, a Bastion post. I run the set. Twice a day I call Command, and twice a day Command doesn't answer. You can ask about anything except that.
  say? !met & role:mechanic :: Mind the oil. You're at {here}, Bastion post, motor pool, such as it is. I keep the trucks running. Anything that moves on our roads went through these hands.
  say? !met & role:medic :: You're at {here}, Bastion post. I'm the medic. Our own come first, then civilians attached, then anyone else. If you're bleeding on my floor, you're anyone else. Sit.
  say? !met :: You're at {here}, a Bastion post. Soldiers, left inside the line when it closed. Command stopped answering. We hold anyway. Keep to the rules and you'll be fine.

conv named.bastion.work
for named:bastion
when !hunted:bastion
topic "How's the shift going?"
prio ask
voice bastion

node start
  say? role:sentry & night :: Night shift. Four hours of looking at a road that looks back. The drones hum out by the line. Something moves in the treeline every twenty minutes and it's always a fox, until it isn't.
  say? role:sentry :: Quiet. Quiet is logged as quiet. Loud is logged as loud. I'm a very simple instrument. Eleven days ago I was a reservist who fixed boilers.
  say? role:radio_operator :: Called Command at oh-six-hundred. Static. Logged the static. Called again at eighteen-hundred. It's a very consistent static. You could set your watch by it.
  say? role:mechanic :: Two vehicles. One runs. The other is a source of parts and comfort. Fuel's the problem. The Red Hand sits on the diesel and charges us for the privilege.
  say? role:medic & persona:3 :: Three sick, one hurt, and one pretending to be sick to get out of the latrine rota. I gave him the latrine rota. It's a known cure.
  say? role:medic :: Quiet in the aid post. Quiet's good. I'm not used to good. Last week was two bites and a man who fell off the wire, and I had bandages for one of them.
  say Same as yesterday. Stand the post, watch the road, log what moves. We're all the line has got, so we hold it. That's the shift. That's every shift.
  > @what Anything that'd make it easier? -> ask
  > @command Does Command ever answer? -> command   if role:radio_operator
  > @how How are things here on the post? -> hub   do call:slot:0
  > @no Carry on. I'll leave you to it. -> hub

node command
  say No. But I keep calling. Twice a day, on the hour, the full call sign. If I stop calling, it's true. Nobody's coming. I know that. I'd just rather not be the one who says it.
  > @help Is there anything I can do? -> ask
  > @back1 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

node ask
  say There's always tasking. A post this size runs short on everything: men for the wire, fuel, batteries for the set. We call them details. Ask properly and I'll tell you if one's live.
  say Pays in Favor with Bastion, and a line in the post log with your name in it. Some of the lads would rather have the line.
  > @take Put me on a detail. What's live? -> hub   do call:slot:1
  > @later Not today. Later, maybe. -> hub

# A sentry's patrol report: the patrol saw nothing in a town that's thick with them (a lie by leaving
# out). Walk in and see (watch), then call it out.
conv named.bastion.word
for named:bastion
when !hunted:bastion
topic "What did the patrol report?"
prio world
voice bastion

bind thick = town:thick_within(2500)
bind lost = news:lost_by(redhand)
bind truck = news:truck

node start
  jump news:lost_by(redhand) -> sold
  jump news:truck -> truck
  jump bound:thick -> cleared
  say? edge :: Drones on their pattern. Loudspeaker at the line said the usual: do not approach. Nobody crossed. Nobody's crossed since Day three. Nobody tried.
  say Patrol went out at oh-seven and came back at eleven-forty, all present. Nothing to report. That's the best thing a patrol report can say.
  > @how How are things here on the post? -> hub   do call:slot:0
  > @back0 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

node cleared
  say Patrol went through {bind:thick} this morning, on the way round. Patrol saw nothing. It's in the log, signed. ~lie:gossip.cleared@thick
  do watch:gossip.cleared@thick:60
  > @catch {bind:thick} is thick with them. -> caught   callout gossip.cleared@thick
  > @how1 And how are things here? -> hub   do call:slot:0
  > @back1 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

node caught
  say Correct. The patrol saw nothing because the patrol didn't go in. It stopped at the edge, looked at the street, and came back round. That part's not in the report.
  say Six men and one magazine each. Now you know why.
  > @how2 And how are things here? -> hub   do call:slot:0
  > @back2 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

node sold
  say The Red Hand lost {bind:lost}. They'll tell you they sold it. They didn't sell anything. They ran, and left their lorry burning on the road. Our patrol logged it. ~truth:gossip.sold@lost
  > @how3 And how are things here? -> hub   do call:slot:0
  > @back3 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

node truck
  say A supply truck didn't arrive. {bind:truck}. Two men in the cab. They're on the list of people we go looking for now. We look for our own. That's the one order we still have.
  > @how4 And how are things here? -> hub   do call:slot:0
  > @back4 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ The Red Hand
conv named.redhand.intro
for named:redhand
when !hunted:redhand
greet
prio world
once
voice redhand

node start
  say? !met & role:toll_man :: Welcome to {here}. Red Hand road, Red Hand rules: you pay the toll, you don't touch what's ours, and everybody sees everything. I'm the toll man. Smile. It's cheaper.
  say? !met & role:lookout :: Saw you from the ridge an hour ago. You walk like you're owed something. You're at {here}, Red Hand camp. Nobody's owed anything here, but everybody owes.
  say? !met & role:mechanic :: Don't lean on that, it's holding the engine up. You're at {here}, Red Hand camp. I keep the lorries going on the boss's diesel. Want something fixed, it's in the book first.
  say? !met & role:cook :: You've found {here} and its kitchen. Red Hand camp. The beans are free for crew and a tin for everyone else. That's not a joke. Nothing here's free unless it's a joke.
  say? !met :: You're at {here}, a Red Hand camp. We take tolls on the roads and keep a book on everyone. Nobody was coming, so we helped ourselves. Behave and you'll do fine.

conv named.redhand.work
for named:redhand
when !hunted:redhand
topic "How's business?"
prio ask
voice redhand

node start
  say? role:toll_man :: Business is people. People are slow today. Slow people pay the same, eventually, plus a little extra for my time. My time's very expensive. Ask anyone who owes me some.
  say? role:lookout & persona:1 :: Business is watching. I'm very good at it. I watched a crow for an hour this morning. The crow lost. It's the most exciting thing that's happened on this road all week.
  say? role:lookout :: Watching the road for Bastion and for the sick, and for anyone carrying something worth a toll. The road's watching back. We've an understanding.
  say? role:mechanic :: Three lorries, two engines, one of me. The maths is against me, and I love maths. Every part I pull is a part somebody owes the book for.
  say? role:cook :: Business is beans. Beans are booming. Crew eat free, everyone else pays a tin a bowl, and the boss takes a cut of the tins. Even the beans pay the toll.
  say Business is business. We take a toll on the roads, we sell what people need, and we write it all down. Nobody was coming. Somebody had to run things, and we were first.
  > @what Anything I can do for business? -> ask
  > @how How are things round here? -> hub   do call:slot:0
  > @no Good luck with it. -> hub

node ask
  say Might be. There's always a little something: fuel for the lorry, a lookout who's skimming, bets to count. Ask me nicely and I'll tell you if there's real money in it.
  say Pays in Favor with the crews. And the book remembers who did us a turn. It remembers everything else too, so you might as well be in it for something good.
  > @take I'm in. What's the little something? -> hub   do call:slot:1
  > @later Not today. Later, maybe. -> hub

# A lookout's tip: a thick town called quiet (a joke lie, to see if you'll go). Walk in and see.
conv named.redhand.word
for named:redhand
when !hunted:redhand
topic "What have the lookouts seen?"
prio world
voice redhand

bind thick = town:thick_within(2500)
bind lost = news:lost_by(bastion)
bind burned = news:burned

node start
  jump news:lost_by(bastion) -> withdrew
  jump news:burned -> burned
  jump bound:thick -> quiet
  say? holds:redhand>=4 :: That we've got more road than ever. More road, more toll, more lookouts sat on hills saying road. Bastion's counting our barriers and getting very cross about it.
  say Nothing. A dog. Bastion pretending not to watch us watching them through the binoculars. We wave. They log it. It's the closest thing to a friendship either side's got.
  > @how How are things round here? -> hub   do call:slot:0
  > @back0 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

node quiet
  say {bind:thick}? Quiet. Dead quiet. Not that kind of dead. Shops nobody's touched, the lot. Go on, have a look. Bring me back a souvenir. ~lie:gossip.quiet@thick
  do watch:gossip.quiet@thick:60
  > @catch {bind:thick} is full of them. -> caught   callout gossip.quiet@thick
  > @how1 And how are things here? -> hub   do call:slot:0
  > @back1 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

node caught
  say Ha! You went. I owe somebody a tin now. Fine: it's thick, wall to wall. Go round by the river. That one's free, because you made me laugh, and that's worth a tin.
  > @how2 And how are things here? -> hub   do call:slot:0
  > @back2 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

node withdrew
  say Bastion lost {bind:lost}. Watched them go through the glasses. Withdrew, they'll call it. Withdrew at a run, with their helmets in their hands. ~truth:gossip.withdrew@lost
  > @how3 And how are things here? -> hub   do call:slot:0
  > @back3 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

node burned
  say {bind:burned} burned. Not us. Burning's waste, and you can't toll ash. Whoever's saying it was us can pay for saying it, with interest. ~truth:gossip.burned@burned
  > @how4 And how are things here? -> hub   do call:slot:0
  > @back4 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ Halcyon
conv named.halcyon.intro
for named:halcyon
when !hunted:halcyon
greet
prio world
once
voice halcyon

node start
  say? !met & role:lab_assistant :: This is {here}, a Halcyon station. I'm a lab assistant. We study the infection, we pay for samples, and we keep a record of everything. Please don't touch the cold boxes.
  say? !met & role:guard :: Stop there. You're at {here}, Halcyon. I keep the door. The lab's the only way this ends, so the door matters more than you or me. State your business.
  say? !met & role:technician :: Mind the cables. You're at {here}, a Halcyon station. I keep the power on. Below sixty percent the cultures die, so I'd rather you didn't trip on anything.
  say? !met :: You're at {here}, a Halcyon station. We're the research team. A cure is the only thing that opens the line, and it is ours to find. Every reading goes in a notebook.

conv named.halcyon.work
for named:halcyon
when !hunted:halcyon
topic "What are you working on?"
prio ask
voice halcyon

node start
  say? role:lab_assistant :: Labelling. Four hundred tubes, each with a sample number, a date and a place. If one label is wrong, a week of work is wrong, and nobody finds out until it matters.
  say? role:guard & persona:2 :: Standing. I stand very well. Eight hours, two doors, one of which doesn't lock. I was a security guard at a shopping centre. The job hasn't changed as much as you'd think.
  say? role:guard :: Watching the door. The door is the most important thing in this station. Everything that matters is behind it. Nobody believes me, until somebody tries it at night.
  say? role:technician :: The generator. It runs at seventy percent. Below sixty, the cultures in the freezers die, and a month of samples goes with them. I check it every hour, day and night.
  say Work. There is a great deal of it. Readings every hour, samples logged and cooled, the numbers read out at the change of shift. The cure is {cure_percent} percent there.
  > @what Anything I can help with? -> ask
  > @how How are things here? -> hub   do call:slot:0
  > @no I'll leave you to it. -> hub

node ask
  say Possibly. A station runs short of fuel for the freezers, batteries for the sensors, hands for the labels at night. We call them small requests. Ask, and I'll check if one is current.
  say We pay in Favor with Halcyon, and your name goes in the notebook as having helped. The notebooks are kept. All of them.
  > @take I'll do it. What's the request? -> hub   do call:slot:1
  > @later Not today. Later, perhaps. -> hub

conv named.halcyon.word
for named:halcyon
when !hunted:halcyon
topic "What's on the board today?"
prio world
voice halcyon

bind over = news:overrun
bind dead = news:leader_dead

node start
  jump news:overrun -> overrun
  jump news:leader_dead -> dead
  say? cure>=75 :: The cure figure. {cure_percent} percent. Someone underlines it every morning on the board by the door. The underline is getting thicker. Nobody admits to doing it.
  say The board says {cure_percent} percent toward the cure. It said that yesterday. Yesterday it said it with less confidence. The number moves when the samples come in.
  > @how How are things here? -> hub   do call:slot:0
  > @back0 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

node overrun
  say {bind:over}. Infection index above eighty. That means the town is theirs now. We'd like samples from there. Nobody would like to fetch them. Both statements are on the board.
  > @how1 And how are things here? -> hub   do call:slot:0
  > @back1 Let me ask you something else. -> hub

node dead
  say {bind:dead}. Deceased. Someone wrote it under the cure figure, small, in pencil. The two numbers don't go together, but there is only one board.
  > @how2 And how are things here? -> hub   do call:slot:0
  > @back2 Let me ask you something else. -> hub
